# Canonical commit identities for the upstream-facing clone.
#
# Ruling: Max, 2026-08-04 12:54 (routed from the fleet identity question).
#   marveen-contrib (this repo, upstream-facing) -> AGENT ID
#   internal repos (marveen, ~/.claude/skills)   -> human persona name
# Rationale: an agent id does not claim a real person. Upstream history is read
# by people outside this fleet, and a persona name there asserts a contributor
# who does not exist.
#
# SCOPE, because this file is easy to over-read: this maps the LOCAL working
# identity only. What authorship a public PR finally carries is decided per
# patch, as part of Andras's GO under the upstream-contribution rule. Nothing
# here creates or approves a publication decision.
#
# Name variants collected 2026-08-04 across marveen, marveen-contrib and
# ~/.claude/skills (author side, --all), so an identity that has not committed
# here yet is still covered the first time it does.

